// Contract between Stampede (the host) and a protocol plugin.
//
// A plugin is an executable that Stampede starts as a child process and
// talks to over gRPC through hashicorp/go-plugin, so a plugin that crashes
// cannot take a worker down with it. One process serves every virtual user
// of a run on that worker: each user opens a session, runs steps in it and
// closes it when it retires.
//
// Configuration travels as JSON: the host renders a step's `with:` block
// (its ${} expressions included) and sends the result; the plugin
// validates it against the JSON Schema it described for that step type.
// What a step returns (its values) is a JSON object too, so checks and
// extractors work on it exactly as on an HTTP response's JSON body.
//
// Durations are nanoseconds.

